    "title": "CHATTER AWAY: Overnight Open Thread",
    "text": "Variety reports :\nAfter just seven days on the big screen, “Spider-Man: Brand New Day” has already supplanted “Toy Story 5” as the highest-grossing movie of the year.\nSony and Marvel’s web-slinging sequel, starring Tom Holland and Zendaya, has generated $1.155 billion to date, including $449 million domestically and $706.3 million internationally. Those ticket sales are above Disney’s “Toy Story 5,” which has earned $1.067 billion since June.\nThe latest milestone builds on the film’s epic theatrical run, which also includes the biggest Tuesday ever at the domestic box office with $42 million, overtaking 2021’s “Spider-Man: No Way Home” with $39 million.\nRead the full article .\n“Spider-Man: Brand New Day” has become the highest-grossing movie of 2026 in just seven days.\n• The film has now grossed $1.15 billion worldwide, including $449M domestically and $706.3M internationally.\n• The year’s previous top grosser was “Toy Story 5,” which has earned… pic.twitter.com/hBNsdfM0GK\n— Variety (@Variety) August 5, 2026",
    "summary": "After just seven days on the big screen, “Spider-Man: Brand New Day” has already supplanted “Toy Story 5” as the highest-grossing movie of the year. Sony and Marvel’s web-slinging sequel, starring Tom Holland and Zendaya, has generated $1.155 billion to date, including $449 million domestically and $706.3 million internationally. Those ticket sales are above Disney’s “Toy Story 5,” which has earned $1.067 billion since June. The latest milestone builds on the film’s epic theatrical run, which also includes the biggest Tuesday ever at the domestic box office with $42 million, overtaking 2021’s “Spider-Man: No Way Home” with $39 million.",
